// @test: typecheck-pass
// @tier: 0
// @level: L1
// @tags: hkt, functor, regression
// @timeout: 5000
// @description: Higher-kinded F<_> type parameter — Functor signature.

/// Higher-kinded types: `F<_>` binds a type constructor of arity 1.
/// This is the canonical Functor signature and is the foundation for
/// every monadic / applicative abstraction in `core/math/category.vr`.
///
/// The body is a `panic`, and that is the point of this file: what is
/// under test is the SIGNATURE — that `F<_>` binds a type constructor and
/// that `F<A>`, `fn(A) -> B` and `F<B>` all resolve against it. A body
/// cannot be written without picking a particular functor.
///
/// It used to read `fa`, which returns `F<A>` where `F<B>` is declared
/// and ignores `f` entirely. That checked clean only because a function's
/// type parameters were not rigid inside its own body: `A` and `B` were
/// ordinary inference variables the body was free to unify with each
/// other. Once they became rigid the stub was correctly rejected, which
/// is how it was found. `panic` has type `Never`, which satisfies any
/// declared return type without claiming anything about `A` or `B`.

fn map<F<_>, A, B>(fa: F<A>, f: fn(A) -> B) -> F<B> {
    panic("signature-only: pick a functor to implement map")
}

mount core.prelude.*;

fn main() {
    print("higher-kinded map parsed and type-checked");
}
